WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Team Room in one minute
One place for project requests,
team discussions and results.
Edited captures of the real open app.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Choose a project
Select your project’s room
from the list at the top.
Each project has its own participants and history.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Set up your team
Menu → Basic team setup
Review the roles and models. Prepare the request, then send it yourself from the current project chat to start.
Your current chat becomes the director. Only five other chats are created.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Manage participants
Menu → Edit members
Add an existing chat from this project, choose its role, then select Save changes.
Hand off active work before removing a participant.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Ask the director
Describe the change and what “done” means.
Enter sends.
Shift+Enter adds a new line.
Input example only. This request was not sent.

6
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Follow the discussion
Read each participant’s questions, replies and progress reports.
The project conversation keeps its original language. Only names are hidden.

7
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Open the work details
Select Show work details for exact files, settings and test evidence.
Read the technical detail when you need it.

8
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
See attached images
Images stay visible outside folded work details.
An actual attachment from the project.

9
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Click to enlarge
Click an image to enlarge it.
Use Close to return.
The real attachment preview window.

10
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Check the connection
Menu → Connection check
Review the project, director and tool status. Follow any warnings.
Use Back up as ZIP to keep a copy.
This captured check includes items that need attention.
